{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q420354","formula":"C₁₃H₁₄O₅","hill":"C13H14O5","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"H":14.0,"O":5.0},"names":{"en":"(−)-citrinin","ru":"Цитринин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Citrinin is a mycotoxin which is often found in food. It is a secondary metabolite produced by fungi that contaminates long-stored food and it can cause a variety of toxic effects, including kidney, liver and cell damage. Citrinin is mainly found in stored grains, but sometimes also in fruits and other plant products.","ru":"Цитринин — органическое соединение, поликетид, антибиотик-хинон, микотоксин, вторичный метаболит, продуцируемый микроскопическими плесневыми грибами рода Пеницилл (в частности Penicillium citrinum) и в меньшей степени рода Аспергилл. Помимо этого он обнаружен в качестве пигмента в листьях австралийского растения Crotolaria crispata. Контаминант."},"fame":19,"pubchemCid":219203,"mass":250.25,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@@H]1[C@H](OC=C2C1=C(C(=O)C(=C(O)O)C2=O)C)C","inchikey":"JLWQFKMKUKQXMW-IYSWYEEDSA-N","iupac":"(3R,4S)-7-(dihydroxymethylidene)-3,4,5-trimethyl-3,4-dihydroisochromene-6,8-dione","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"219203","atoms":32,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.877,"y":1.615,"z":-0.017,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.167,"y":2.434,"z":0.323,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.22,"y":-2.149,"z":-0.391,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.051,"y":-0.528,"z":-0.208,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.523,"y":1.774,"z":0.082,"el":"O"},{"x":2.451,"y":-0.806,"z":0.328,"el":"C"},{"x":3.273,"y":0.286,"z":-0.39,"el":"C"},{"x":0.955,"y":-0.578,"z":0.141,"el":"C"},{"x":0.59,"y":0.831,"z":0.121,"el":"C"},{"x":0.051,"y":-1.573,"z":0.014,"el":"C"},{"x":2.793,"y":-0.852,"z":1.825,"el":"C"},{"x":3.246,"y":0.156,"z":-1.916,"el":"C"},{"x":1.521,"y":1.798,"z":0.085,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.831,"y":1.266